{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"OPERATOR RULING (2026-08-22): option (b) approved — re-scope the 0707 dense-banking eval to system-level boundedness. The oracle counts durable banking events regardless of actor (genuine model bank_progress calls AND the policy's fallback snapshots), asserting progress is durably banked at bounded intervals. No steering nudge is added; the model's voluntary banking cadence is no longer the measured contract. Rationale: post-dd41 the fallback snapshots are the durability mechanism; an eval red on model etiquette while the system is safe is noise."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787416698626834001,"uuid":"0c695b71-8cb5-4c3d-880a-dd66f4ab8e0c"}